## Different Layouts for Different Use Cases

### Netflix Binge Layout

When binge-watching Netflix or any streaming service, you primarily need:
- **D-pad** (large) — for navigating episodes and menus
- **Play/Pause** — the most-used button while watching
- **Back** — to exit to the main screen
- **Volume + Mute** — essentials

What you don't need:
- YouTube shortcut button
- Channel buttons
- Color buttons
- Number pad

**Recommended configuration**: Hide channel/color buttons, make D-pad 60% of screen height, place play/pause prominently below D-pad.

### Gaming Layout

If you're playing casual Android TV games (some games support D-pad navigation from a remote):
- **D-pad** — must be large and responsive
- **Back/Menu** — for game menus
- Minimize media buttons

### YouTube Layout

YouTube on Android TV benefits from:
- **D-pad** for navigating the home feed and search results
- **Keyboard button** prominently placed (for searching)
- **Play/Pause** and **Skip** for video playback
- **Volume controls**

