## Why Customizable Layouts Beat Physical Remotes

Let's be direct about it:

| Feature | Physical Remote | Customizable Phone Remote |
|---|---|---|
| Button layout | Fixed by manufacturer | Fully customizable |
| Button size | Fixed, often small | Adjustable |
| Unused buttons | Always visible | Can be hidden |
| One-hand optimization | Usually no | Yes |
| Accessibility (large buttons) | Rare/expensive models | Standard feature |
| Night use (backlit) | Some remotes only | Always (phone screen) |
| Replacement cost | $20–$50 | Free |
| Learning curve | Immediate | Minutes to customize |

The physical remote wins only on: tactile button feel, dedicated hardware (doesn't need charging), and simplicity for non-tech users. Everything else tilts toward a customizable phone remote.

